1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:08,800
Every suspicious message, unfamiliar link, and deceptive payment request forces someone to make a decision. But recognizing digital fraud is not always easy.

2
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:18,500
Meet SuSagi Guardian, a privacy-conscious cybersecurity assistant designed to help people understand threats and make safer decisions.

3
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:38,500
SuSagi examines not just suspicious keywords, but context, requested actions, and supporting evidence. An unverified prize announcement is fundamentally different from a demand for money or banking credentials.

4
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:52,800
Dedicated security modules examine deceptive URLs, suspicious payment requests, and other digital threat indicators, translating technical findings into understandable protective guidance.

5
00:00:53,500 --> 00:01:12,500
Activating compatible local AI models unlocks conversational intelligence and speech understanding. SuSagi uses Llama for contextual explanations and Whisper to transform supported speech into analyzable text.

6
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:32,500
At its core, SuSagi couples a deterministic Contextual Security Engine with Meta's ExecuTorch runtime on Arm64. Messages decompose into structured intent and requested actions, delivering sub-four-millisecond risk evaluation entirely within the local device boundary.

7
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:46,800
SuSagi combines dedicated security logic with an edge AI architecture, prioritizing understandable evidence, responsible risk assessment, and privacy-conscious processing across 318 verified unit tests.

8
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:58,000
SuSagi Guardian is designed to make cybersecurity more accessible, intelligent, and understandable. Think before you click. Know before you trust.
